---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import MedalBadge from '../../components/MedalBadge.astro';

const allSystems = await getCollection('systems');

// Define the 6809 family systems
const system6809Slugs = [
  'tandy-coco3', 'dragon-data-dragon-32', 'thomson-to7', 'trs-80-coco'
];

const systems = system6809Slugs
  .map(slug => allSystems.find(s => s.slug === slug))
  .filter(Boolean)
  .filter(s => s.data.status !== 'vault')
  .sort((a, b) => {
    const tierOrder = { platinum: 0, gold: 1, silver: 2, bronze: 3 };
    const tierA = tierOrder[a.data.medal_tier] ?? 4;
    const tierB = tierOrder[b.data.medal_tier] ?? 4;
    if (tierA !== tierB) return tierA - tierB;
    return (b.data.total_lessons || 0) - (a.data.total_lessons || 0);
  });

const totalLessons = systems.reduce((sum, s) => sum + (s.data.total_lessons || 0), 0);
const totalGames = systems.reduce((sum, s) => sum + (s.data.total_games || 0), 0);

// Group by medal tier
const platinum = systems.filter(s => s.data.medal_tier === 'platinum');
const gold = systems.filter(s => s.data.medal_tier === 'gold');
const silver = systems.filter(s => s.data.medal_tier === 'silver');
const bronze = systems.filter(s => s.data.medal_tier === 'bronze');
---

<Layout title="6809 Architecture Track | Code Like It's 198x">
  <main class="min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-b from-gray-900 to-black text-green-400">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 py-12">
      <header class="mb-12">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-4">
          <a href="/tracks/" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-green-400 transition">
            ← Back to Tracks
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-6">
          <div class="text-6xl">🔺</div>
          <div>
            <h1 class="text-5xl font-bold mb-2 text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-400 to-indigo-400">
              Motorola 6809 Family
            </h1>
            <p class="text-xl text-gray-300">
              The most advanced 8-bit processor architecture ever created
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-4 gap-6 mb-12">
        <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg p-6 border-2 border-gray-700">
          <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-white">{systems.length}</div>
          <div class="text-gray-400">Systems</div>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg p-6 border-2 border-gray-700">
          <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-white">{totalLessons.toLocaleString()}</div>
          <div class="text-gray-400">Total Lessons</div>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg p-6 border-2 border-gray-700">
          <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-white">{totalGames.toLocaleString()}</div>
          <div class="text-gray-400">Games to Build</div>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg p-6 border-2 border-gray-700">
          <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-white">1978-1995</div>
          <div class="text-gray-400">Era Covered</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg p-8 mb-12 border-2 border-gray-700">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-white">About the 6809 Architecture</h2>
        <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none text-gray-300">
          <p class="mb-4">
            The Motorola 6809, introduced in 1978, represents the pinnacle of 8-bit processor design. 
            Created as the successor to the 6800, it featured advanced capabilities that wouldn't become 
            common until 16-bit processors emerged. The 6809 combined elegant architecture with powerful 
            features, earning it recognition as potentially the best 8-bit processor ever designed.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2 text-green-400">Advanced 8-Bit Features</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4">
            <li><strong>Two 8-bit accumulators:</strong> A and B registers can combine as 16-bit D register</li>
            <li><strong>Advanced addressing modes:</strong> 59 different addressing combinations</li>
            <li><strong>Position-independent code:</strong> Natural support for relocatable programs</li>
            <li><strong>Dual stack pointers:</strong> Hardware (S) and user (U) stack separation</li>
            <li><strong>Powerful index registers:</strong> X and Y with full 16-bit arithmetic</li>
            <li><strong>Direct page register:</strong> Fast access to any 256-byte page</li>
            <li><strong>Hardware multiplication:</strong> 8×8 multiply instruction</li>
          </ul>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2 text-green-400">Orthogonal Design Philosophy</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4">
            <li><strong>Consistent instruction format:</strong> Most operations work with all registers</li>
            <li><strong>Register exchange:</strong> Transfer data between any two registers</li>
            <li><strong>Auto-increment/decrement:</strong> Built-in pointer manipulation</li>
            <li><strong>Conditional branching:</strong> 16 different condition tests</li>
            <li><strong>Block operations:</strong> Efficient memory and I/O transfers</li>
          </ul>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2 text-green-400">System Variations</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li><strong>TRS-80 Color Computer:</strong> Radio Shack's 6809 home computer line</li>
            <li><strong>Dragon 32/64:</strong> Welsh-built alternative with Extended Color BASIC</li>
            <li><strong>Thomson TO7/TO8:</strong> French educational computers with light pen</li>
            <li><strong>Tandy CoCo 3:</strong> Advanced model with GIME graphics and OS-9</li>
            <li><strong>6809E variant:</strong> Enhanced version with additional control signals</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6 text-white">Learning Path</h2>
        
        {gold.length > 0 && (
          <div class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span>🥇</span>
              <span class="text-gray-300">Gold Tier - Advanced 6809 Mastery (2,048 lessons each)</span>
            </h3>
            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
              {gold.map(system => (
                <a href={`/systems/${system.slug}/`} class="block bg-gray-900 rounded-lg p-6 border-2 border-gray-800 hover:border-green-400 transition-all">
                  <div class="flex items-start justify-between mb-3">
                    <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">{system.data.name || system.data.title}</h4>
                    <MedalBadge tier={system.data.medal_tier} size="small" />
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-3">{system.data.year || system.data.release_year} • {system.data.manufacturer}</p>
                  <div class="flex gap-4 text-xs text-gray-500">
                    <span>{system.data.total_lessons} lessons</span>
                    <span>{system.data.total_games} games</span>
                    <span>{system.data.estimated_duration}</span>
                  </div>
                </a>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        )}

        {silver.length > 0 && (
          <div class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span>🥈</span>
              <span class="text-gray-300">Silver Tier - Solid Foundation (1,024 lessons each)</span>
            </h3>
            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
              {silver.map(system => (
                <a href={`/systems/${system.slug}/`} class="block bg-gray-900 rounded-lg p-6 border-2 border-gray-800 hover:border-green-400 transition-all">
                  <div class="flex items-start justify-between mb-3">
                    <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">{system.data.name || system.data.title}</h4>
                    <MedalBadge tier={system.data.medal_tier} size="small" />
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-3">{system.data.year || system.data.release_year} • {system.data.manufacturer}</p>
                  <div class="flex gap-4 text-xs text-gray-500">
                    <span>{system.data.total_lessons} lessons</span>
                    <span>{system.data.total_games} games</span>
                  </div>
                </a>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        )}

        {bronze.length > 0 && (
          <div class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span>🥉</span>
              <span class="text-gray-300">Bronze Tier - Quick Start (512 lessons each)</span>
            </h3>
            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
              {bronze.map(system => (
                <a href={`/systems/${system.slug}/`} class="block bg-gray-900 rounded-lg p-6 border-2 border-gray-800 hover:border-green-400 transition-all">
                  <div class="flex items-start justify-between mb-3">
                    <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">{system.data.name || system.data.title}</h4>
                    <MedalBadge tier={system.data.medal_tier} size="small" />
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-3">{system.data.year || system.data.release_year} • {system.data.manufacturer}</p>
                  <div class="flex gap-4 text-xs text-gray-500">
                    <span>{system.data.total_lessons} lessons</span>
                    <span>{system.data.total_games} games</span>
                  </div>
                </a>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        )}
      </div>

      <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-900 to-indigo-900 rounded-lg p-8 border-2 border-purple-700">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-white">Recommended Learning Path</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-gray-300">
          <div class="flex gap-4">
            <div class="text-2xl">1️⃣</div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">Begin with TRS-80 Color Computer</h3>
              <p class="text-sm">Start with the original CoCo to learn 6809 fundamentals and Extended Color BASIC. The straightforward architecture and excellent documentation make it perfect for understanding 6809 concepts.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex gap-4">
            <div class="text-2xl">2️⃣</div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">Explore Regional Variations with Dragon 32</h3>
              <p class="text-sm">Discover how the Welsh Dragon computer implemented 6809 architecture differently. Learn about regional computing history and alternative approaches to the same processor.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex gap-4">
            <div class="text-2xl">3️⃣</div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">Master Advanced Features with Thomson TO7</h3>
              <p class="text-sm">Experience the French educational computer's unique light pen interface and sophisticated graphics. Understand how 6809's capabilities enabled innovative user interfaces.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex gap-4">
            <div class="text-2xl">4️⃣</div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">Achieve Mastery with Tandy CoCo 3</h3>
              <p class="text-sm">Progress to the most advanced 6809 system with GIME graphics, OS-9 multitasking, and professional development capabilities. Experience workstation-class computing on 8-bit hardware.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg p-8 mt-8 border-2 border-gray-700">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-white">Why Master 6809 Assembly?</h3>
        <div class="text-gray-300 space-y-3">
          <p>
            The 6809 represents the peak of 8-bit processor evolution, offering features that weren't 
            seen again until 32-bit processors became common. Learning 6809 assembly teaches advanced 
            programming concepts in an understandable context, without the complexity of modern processors.
          </p>
          <p>
            The processor's orthogonal design and advanced addressing modes make it an excellent 
            teaching platform for understanding how elegant architecture design simplifies programming. 
            The 6809's position-independent code capabilities and dual stack system demonstrate 
            concepts crucial for modern operating system development.
          </p>
          <p>
            Programming 6809 systems reveals how hardware and software co-evolved during the transition 
            from 8-bit to 16-bit computing. The techniques learned here apply directly to embedded 
            systems development and provide deep insights into computer architecture principles 
            that remain relevant today.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg p-8 mt-8 border-2 border-gray-700">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-white">Cultural Computing Perspectives</h3>
        <div class="text-gray-300 space-y-3">
          <p>
            The 6809 track offers unique insights into how different countries and companies 
            approached computing in the 1980s. From Radio Shack's mass market strategy to Wales' 
            technological ambitions to France's educational computing initiatives, each system 
            tells a different story about regional computing development.
          </p>
          <p>
            These systems demonstrate that technical excellence doesn't always translate to commercial 
            success. The 6809's superior architecture competed against the more successful but simpler 
            6502 and Z80 processors, providing valuable lessons about technology adoption and 
            market dynamics that remain relevant in today's tech industry.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>